The Solana NFT scene has seen a lot of movement the last couple of weeks. Pack products stayed active, a few established collections kept shipping, and physical-linked drops continued to draw attention.

A quick look at some of what’s been moving with #SolanaRecap

@yugalabs’ Mudwater Packs (BAYC trading cards) has been one of the more active collections on Solana recently. Digital packs and cards live on Solana with physical cards in a vault. BAYC holders can claim 10 packs each and Mutants 2, with claims open until January 2027. The set has 120 designs plus foil and serialized variants, and sealed packs, boxes, and cases trade separately.

@Collector_Crypt had a standout stretch after https://t.co/A004XZImvr integrated its randomized packs and marketplace. The platform recorded a record day with heavy pack opening volume across graded Pokémon, One Piece, and sports cards tokenized on Solana. It remains one of the more consistent volume drivers in the Solana collectibles space.

@MadLads (by @Backpack) continues to act as one of the steadier blue-chip PFPs on the chain. Backpack-linked and long-running, it still sees regular trading and remains a reference point for Solana NFT liquidity.

@Claynosaurz shared its roadmap live on Rarible Unsealed this week. The animated series is the top priority: the team is making the first episode in-house while an outside studio produces the full series. A mobile game already built with Gameloft will launch alongside the show, aimed at a new audience of kids aged 6 to 12. On the physical side, a blind box recently launched to retail, and new products for the niche collectibles market in Japan and the US are on the way. The micro-episodes are already on Amazon Prime, and longer episodes are in development.

@jurassicfi brought real fossils to the same stream. Its tokenized Triceratops skull, Deaton, is in Arizona, and the team is planning a museum event around it. Holders own contractual rights to a share of Deaton’s final sale, proportional to their stake. Next up is a dinosaur-only gacha where you can pull real fossil grails like T-Rex pieces, Triceratops bones and raptor claws, with Pokémon cards filling out the rest of the pool.

@rarible hosted the Unsealed Dino Special, debuting a revamped Gacha with around nine machines across Pokémon, Lorcana, sports and more. New card search shows which gacha each card is in, and a buyback option returns funds to your wallet instantly. The new $65 Dino Pack (one dollar for each of the 65 million years) was ripped 12 times live, and every card went to a trivia winner in the chat. Rarible’s Gacha is also coming to the Seeker phone soon. The Dino Pack is live for a limited time: https://t.co/AkbBNtvHZ5

@TrencherStudio celebrated 1.5 years of the project in late October. Artist @grizzle_art was named a finalist for the 2026 Solana Artist Award, and the project has continued expanding its TCG and physical presence after the earlier Tokyo event and Shibuya Crossing billboard. The team has also been sharing behind-the-scenes work on character models, trading cards, and animations.

@crittersquest launched Season 2 in early October. The update focused on new systems, stronger PvP (including town attacks and raids), and an in-game guide to help players with workshops and gameplay. Season 1 remains active, with holders still using Master Editions and Clones inside the on-chain 4X loop.

